@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To Provisioning License Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account integration to provisioning and License Management works properly.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products with their respective field values
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                         |
	| DXP Backup                             |
	| DXP Non-Production                     |
	| Portal Production                      |
	| Platinum Subscription                  |
	| Gold Subscription                      |
	| Limited Subscription                   |
	| Enterprise Search for DXP Cloud - Prod |
	| Commerce Subscription Production       |
	| Developer Services                     |
	| Analytics Cloud Basic                  |
	| Enterprise Search - Production         |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PROKORKORPRO |

Scenario: Generate new DXP license via provisioning site
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki via the provisioning site

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PROKORKORPRO                         |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Product                | DXP Production                             | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId}                 | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                                  | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                            | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                          | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticEndDate}   | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDate} | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | DXP Production |
	| Provisioned  | 1              |
	| Status       | ACTIVE         |
	When I click on the "DXP Production" subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on provisioned link for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |

Scenario: Generate new DXP and Portal license via provisioning site
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP and Portal project from koroneiki via the provisioning site

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PROKORKORPRO                         |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I rename the first product purchase id variable
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for "Portal Production"
	And I rename the second product purchase id variable
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Product                | DXP Production                             | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId1}                | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                                  | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                            | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                          | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticEndDate}   | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDate} | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Portal Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Product                | Portal Production              | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 6.2 EE                         | |
	| Type                   | Portal Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId2}    | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                      | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F              | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "Portal Production 6.2 EE" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | Portal Production 6.2 EE      |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticEndDate}   | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDate} | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | DXP Production |
	| Provisioned  | 1              |
	| Status       | ACTIVE         |
	When I click on the "DXP Production" subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should not be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "Portal Production 6.2 EE"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should not be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "Portal Production 6.2 EE"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on provisioned link for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | DXP Production 7.2            |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should not be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "Portal Production 6.2 EE"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "Portal Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Portal Production |
	| Provisioned  | 1                 |
	| Status       | ACTIVE            |
	When I click on the "Portal Production" subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | Portal Production 6.2 EE      |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should not be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "DXP Production 7.2"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Portal Production" subscription link
	And I click on subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | Portal Production 6.2 EE      |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should not be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "DXP Production 7.2"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Portal Production" subscription link
	And I click on provisioned link for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORPRO                        |
	| Name            | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product         | Portal Production 6.2 EE      |
	| Type            | Production                    |
	And I should not be able to view the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and product "DXP Production 7.2"

Scenario: Deactivate new DXP license via provisioning site
	Testing the ability to generate and deactivate new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki via the provisioning site

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PROKORKORPRO                         |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Product                | DXP Production                             | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId}                 | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                                  | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                            | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                          | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	And I click on the license with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I click on the deactivate link
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should not be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | DXP Production |
	| Provisioned  | 0              |
	| Status       | ACTIVE         |

